# Cloudflare Pages routing for the SPA (built with base /mos/ into a flat dist/).
# The app references its files under /mos/, which have no real file on Pages, so these rules
# rewrite them onto the flat output. A /mos/ file missing here is served as index.html (text/html)
# and breaks: a .js asset renders the app blank, sw.js fails to register.
# Every other /mos/ path (deep links) is served index.html by Pages' built-in SPA fallback, which
# holds only while dist/ has no 404.html. A `/mos/* /index.html 200` rule is rejected by Pages as
# an infinite loop, so it cannot replace that fallback.
# Exact rules come before the splat rule (Pages matches them on its fast path).
/                         /mos/                    302
/mos/sw.js                /sw.js                   200
/mos/manifest.webmanifest /manifest.webmanifest    200
# Pages strips .html: an /offline.html target would answer 308, not the page the worker precaches.
/mos/offline.html         /offline                 200
/mos/assets/*             /assets/:splat           200
